pages.today=()=>`${head('Good morning, Vadym.','A little clarity for the day ahead.',btn('Customize','customize-today','sliders')+btn('Quick capture','quick-capture','plus','primary'),'MONDAY, NOVEMBER 16')}${!state.setup&&!state.setupDismissed?`<div class="setup-banner"><div class="banner-icon">${icon('spark')}</div><div class="grow"><h3>Your workspace is ready. Let’s make your tools ready, too.</h3><p>Use Claude Code directly, or connect CodeMie. You can keep exploring as you set up.</p></div>${linkBtn('Finish setup','onboarding.html','arrow','primary')}<button class="icon-btn dismiss-banner" data-action="dismiss-setup" aria-label="Dismiss setup banner">${icon('close')}</button></div>`:''}<div class="today-layout"><div><section class="hero"><div class="hero-text"><div class="kicker accent">YOUR DAY, CONNECTED</div><h2>Space to think.<br>Context to move forward.</h2><p>You have <strong>3 meetings</strong> and <strong>90 minutes of focus time</strong>.<br>Your morning brief has the context you’ll need.</p><button class="text-link mt" data-action="morning-brief">Read your morning brief ${icon('arrow')}</button></div><div class="hero-orbit" aria-hidden="true"><div class="orb-center">${icon('spark')}</div><i class="orb-dot"></i></div></section><div class="stats-strip"><a href="inbox.html" class="panel stat-mini"><div class="stat-icon">${icon('inbox')}</div><div><div class="num">${Math.max(0,4-state.archived.length)} <span class="small dim">items</span></div><p>Need your attention</p></div></a><a href="calendar.html" class="panel stat-mini"><div class="stat-icon">${icon('calendar')}</div><div><div class="num">3 <span class="small dim">meetings</span></div><p>On today’s calendar</p></div></a><a href="knowledge.html" class="panel stat-mini"><div class="stat-icon">${icon('book')}</div><div><div class="num">${24+state.documents.length} <span class="small dim">pages</span></div><p>Growing with you</p></div></a></div>${panel('A few things to move forward',taskItems.map(([id,title,sub,href,type])=>`<div class="task-row"><button class="check-task ${state.tasks[id]?'checked':''}" data-action="task:${id}" aria-label="${state.tasks[id]?'Reopen':'Complete'} ${title}">${state.tasks[id]?icon('check'):''}</button><a class="grow" href="${href}"><h3 class="${state.tasks[id]?'done':''}">${title}</h3><p>${sub}</p></a>${tag(type)}<a class="icon-btn" aria-label="Open ${title}" href="${href}">${icon('chevron')}</a></div>`).join(''),linkBtn('View inbox','inbox.html','','ghost sm'),'check')}<div class="section-title"><h2>From your workspace</h2><a class="text-link small" href="plugins.html">Explore plugins ${icon('arrow')}</a></div><div class="grid2 widget-area">${state.widgets.includes('github')&&state.plugins.github?.enabled?`<section class="panel widget-card" data-widget-slot="github"><div class="between"><div class="widget-heading">${icon('github')}GitHub, at a glance</div>${tag('PLUGIN','purple')}</div><div class="widget-number">2 <span class="small muted">reviews waiting</span></div><p>A useful place to start after your morning sync.</p><div class="line"></div><div class="between small"><span class="success">${icon('check')} All checks passing</span><a class="text-link" href="plugin.html?id=github">Open ${icon('arrow')}</a></div></section>`:''}${state.widgets.includes('knowledge')?`<section class="panel widget-card" data-widget-slot="knowledge"><div class="between"><div class="widget-heading">${icon('book')}Your knowledge garden</div>${tag('LOCAL','green')}</div><div class="widget-number">${state.notesSaved?'5':'4'} <span class="small muted">new connections</span></div><p>Your meeting notes are becoming useful context.</p><div class="line"></div><div class="between small"><span class="dim">Updated 12 minutes ago</span><a class="text-link" href="knowledge-graph.html">Explore graph ${icon('arrow')}</a></div></section>`:''}${state.widgets.includes('routines')&&state.plugins.scheduler?.enabled?`<section class="panel widget-card" data-widget-slot="routines"><div class="widget-heading">${icon('automation')}A calmer morning</div><p style="margin:12px 0">Your brief is ready. Three decisions, two follow-ups, one clear place to begin.</p><button class="text-link small" data-action="morning-brief">Open brief ${icon('arrow')}</button></section>`:''}${state.widgets.includes('focus')&&state.plugins['focus-card']?.enabled?`<section class="panel widget-card" data-widget-slot="focus"><div class="widget-heading">${icon('heart')}Focus card</div><div class="widget-number">90 <span class="small muted">minutes protected</span></div><p>From your own Echo-format plugin.</p><button class="text-link small mt" data-action="focus-session">Start a focus session ${icon('arrow')}</button></section>`:''}</div><div class="section-title"><h2>Recently in your knowledge</h2><a class="text-link small" href="knowledge.html">View all</a></div><div class="panel panel-pad">${[['Workspace principles','Personal knowledge · Updated today'],['Design review · Decisions','Workspace redesign · Friday'],['A guide to better meeting notes','Learning garden · Thursday']].map(([t,s])=>`<a class="knowledge-item" href="knowledge.html?doc=${encodeURIComponent(t)}">${icon('file')}<span class="grow"><strong>${t}</strong><span class="dim" style="display:block;font-size:10px">${s}</span></span>${icon('chevron')}</a>`).join('')}</div></div><aside class="today-rail stack">${state.widgets.includes('agenda')?panel('On your calendar',graphReady('calendar')?`<div class="agenda-day"><time>10:00</time><div class="agenda-event next"><div class="between"><h3>Product sync</h3>${tag('UP NEXT','purple')}</div><p>30 min · Microsoft Teams</p><div class="flex mt"><div class="avatars"><span class="avatar peach">AM</span><span class="avatar blue">JT</span><span class="avatar">+2</span></div><a class="text-link small" href="meeting.html">Prepare ${icon('arrow')}</a></div></div><time>11:30</time><div class="agenda-event"><h3>Workspace design review</h3><p>45 min · Microsoft Teams</p></div><time>14:00</time><div class="agenda-event"><h3>Weekly planning</h3><p>30 min · Microsoft Teams</p></div></div><div style="padding:0 20px 20px"><div class="focus-block">${icon('sun')}90 min of focus · 14:30–16:00</div></div>`:empty('Connect your calendar','Bring your Microsoft 365 agenda here.',linkBtn('Connect Microsoft 365','settings-connections.html','','sm'),'calendar'),'<a class="text-link small" href="calendar.html">Open</a>','calendar'):''}${panel('Pick up where you left off',`<div style="padding:0 20px 20px"><a class="meeting-art" style="display:flex;height:85px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--accent-soft);align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--accent)" href="meeting.html">${icon('video')}</a><h3 style="font-size:12px;margin:12px 0 5px">Workspace design review</h3><p class="small">Friday, 13 Nov · 42 minutes</p><div class="between mt">${tag('Minutes ready','green')}<a class="text-link small" href="meeting.html">Review ${icon('arrow')}</a></div></div>`,'','video')}<div class="notice"><div class="flex mb" style="margin-bottom:7px">${icon('shield')}<strong>Your context stays yours.</strong></div>Your notes live on this device. Choose the profile and sources for every AI conversation.<a href="settings-privacy.html" class="text-link" style="display:block;margin-top:9px">Review your permissions ${icon('arrow')}</a></div></aside></div>`;
const settingsLinks=[['settings','General'],['settings-ai','AI profiles'],['settings-connections','Connections'],['settings-setup','Setup & tools'],['settings-appearance','Appearance'],['settings-privacy','Privacy & permissions']];
function settingsShell(body){return `${head('Settings','A workspace that works your way.')}<div class="settings-layout"><nav class="settings-nav" aria-label="Settings sections">${settingsLinks.map(([id,label])=>`<a href="${route(id)}" class="${page===id?'active':''}" ${page===id?'aria-current="page"':''}>${label}</a>`).join('')}<div class="kicker">Extensions</div><a href="plugins.html?tab=installed">Installed plugins</a><a href="plugin-studio.html">Developer tools</a></nav><div class="settings-section">${body}</div></div>`}
const settingRow=(title,desc,control)=>`<div class="setting-row"><div class="grow"><h3>${title}</h3><p>${desc}</p></div>${control}</div>`;
pages.settings=()=>settingsShell(`<h2>General</h2><p class="intro">Small details that make the workspace feel like yours.</p><div class="panel">${settingRow('Workspace name','A personal place for your notes, conversations and routines.',btn(esc(state.workspaceName||'Personal workspace'),'workspace-name','edit'))}${settingRow('Open at login','Be ready for your day, without another thing to remember.',toggle('launch','Open at login',state.launch))}${settingRow('Notifications','Only useful updates: upcoming meetings, ready notes and requests for you.',toggle('notifications','Enable notifications',state.notifications))}${settingRow('Start page','Where you land when you open the app.',`<select data-preference="startPage" aria-label="Start page">${['Today','Calendar','Chat','Knowledge'].map(v=>`<option ${state.startPage===v?'selected':''}>${v}</option>`).join('')}</select>`)}${settingRow('Time zone','Used for your calendar and scheduled routines.',`<select data-preference="timezone" aria-label="Time zone"><option>Europe/Kyiv</option><option ${state.timezone==='Europe/London'?'selected':''}>Europe/London</option><option ${state.timezone==='America/New_York'?'selected':''}>America/New_York</option></select>`)}</div><div class="section-title"><h2>Workspace data</h2>${tag('ON THIS DEVICE','green')}</div><div class="panel">${settingRow('Your local workspace','Notes, preferences and plugin data stay in your own workspace folder.',btn('View folders','view-folders','folder'))}${settingRow('Export your workspace','Download the sample workspace and preferences as JSON.',btn('Export','export-workspace','download'))}${settingRow('About CodeMie Connect','Workspace concept · Based on Connect 2.1.1 and Echo 0.9.9.',btn('About','about','info'))}</div><div class="notice mt">${icon('spark')} <strong>CodeMie is optional.</strong> Use your Claude Code subscription directly, and connect the platform only when you need it. <a href="settings-ai.html" class="text-link">Manage AI profiles</a></div>`);
const setupTabs=[['installation','Installation'],['tools','AI tools'],['desktop','Desktop connections'],['health','Health'],['logs','Activity log'],['updates','Updates']];
pages['settings-setup']=()=>settingsShell(`<h2>Setup & tools</h2><p class="intro">Everything from the current Connect app, in one dedicated place.</p><nav class="tabs" aria-label="Setup sections">${setupTabs.map(([id,label])=>`<button class="tab ${transient.setupTab===id?'active':''}" data-action="setup-tab:${id}">${label}</button>`).join('')}</nav>${setupBody()}`);
function setupBody(){switch(transient.setupTab){case 'tools':return `<div class="between mb"><div><h3>AI coding tools</h3><p class="small">Install and maintain the tools you use outside the app.</p></div>${btn('Refresh','refresh-tools','refresh','sm')}</div><div class="panel">${settingRow('Claude Code',`Anthropic’s terminal assistant · ${state.claude?'Installed · detected on this device':'Not installed'}`,`<div class="flex">${tag(state.claude?'Ready':'Not installed',state.claude?'green':'')}${btn(state.claude?'Manage':'Install',state.claude?'manage-tool:claude':'install-tool:claude',state.claude?'more':'download','sm')}</div>`)}${settingRow('Codex CLI','An additional coding tool. Installation does not add an AI profile.',btn(state.codex?'Manage':'Install',state.codex?'manage-tool:codex':'install-tool:codex',state.codex?'more':'download','sm'))}${settingRow('Gemini CLI','An additional coding tool. Configure its provider separately.',btn(state.gemini?'Manage':'Install',state.gemini?'manage-tool:gemini':'install-tool:gemini',state.gemini?'more':'download','sm'))}</div><div class="notice mt">Tool management keeps the current install, update and remove flows. Workspace AI profiles are managed separately in <a class="text-link" href="settings-ai.html">AI profiles</a>.</div>`;
case 'desktop':return `<div class="panel panel-pad"><div class="flex"><div class="round-icon">${icon('monitor')}</div><div class="grow"><h3>Claude Desktop</h3><p class="small">Connect the desktop client through the CodeMie proxy.</p></div>${tag(state.desktop?'Connected':'Disconnected',state.desktop?'green':'')}</div><div class="line"></div><p class="small mb">${state.desktop?'Claude Desktop uses the CodeMie gateway. Quit and reopen Claude Desktop after changing this connection.':'This connection is optional. It needs a configured CodeMie account; direct Claude Code works independently.'}</p><div class="flex wrap">${btn(state.desktop?'Reconnect':'Connect','desktop-connect','link','primary')}${btn('Restart connection','desktop-restart','refresh')}${btn('Disconnect','desktop-disconnect','close','ghost')}</div></div><details class="mt"><summary>What happens when I disconnect?</summary><p>The CodeMie connection is removed from Claude Desktop. The proxy keeps running. Restart Claude Desktop to apply the change. Connect again to restore the connection.</p></details>`;
case 'health':return `<div class="between mb"><div><h3>Your environment</h3><p class="small">Clear results, with a next step when something needs attention.</p></div>${btn('Check everything again','run-health','refresh','primary')}</div>${state.health==='idle'?'<div class="notice mb">Run a check to see the current demo environment status.</div>':''}<div class="panel">${[['Claude Code',state.claude?'Detected and executable':'Not installed',state.claude],['AI profile',state.mode==='direct'?'Direct account · ready':'CodeMie project · '+(state.setup?'signed in':'setup needed'),state.mode==='direct'||state.setup],['CodeMie CLI',state.cli?'Runtime and PATH look good':'Optional for your direct profile',state.cli||state.mode==='direct'],['Desktop connection',state.desktop?'Gateway reachable':'Optional · not connected',true],['Microsoft 365',state.graph==='connected'?'Account connected · '+state.graphScopes.length+' capabilities':state.graph==='expired'?'Sign-in expired':state.graph==='blocked'?'Tenant approval needed':'Not connected',state.graph==='connected']].map(([a,b,ok])=>settingRow(a,b,tag(ok?'Healthy':'Needs attention',ok?'green':'amber'))).join('')}</div><div class="flex mt">${btn('View diagnostic details','diagnostics','terminal')}${linkBtn('Activity log','settings-setup.html#logs','list')}</div>`;
case 'logs':return `<div class="between mb"><div><h3>What Connect ran</h3><p class="small">A transparent record of setup and tool operations.</p></div>${btn('Copy all','copy-logs','copy','sm')}</div><div class="panel panel-pad">${state.logs.map(l=>`<details><summary><span class="mono dim">${l.at}</span> &nbsp;<span class="mono">${esc(l.cmd)}</span> &nbsp;${tag(l.status==='success'?'Success':'Failed',l.status==='success'?'green':'red')}</summary><pre class="codebox">${esc(l.result)}</pre></details>`).join('')}</div><div class="notice mt">Sample command output only. The prototype never starts a terminal or runs a system command.</div>`;
case 'updates':return `<div class="panel">${settingRow('CodeMie Connect',state.appUpdated?'You’re on the latest demo version.':'A new app version is available. Your workspace and preferences will be kept.',btn(state.appUpdated?'Up to date':'Review update','app-update','download','sm'))}${settingRow('CodeMie CLI',state.cliUpdated?'CLI update completed.':'Background CLI updates remain available here.',btn(state.cliUpdated?'Up to date':'Update CLI','cli-update','refresh','sm'))}${settingRow('Plugin updates','Review new permissions before applying plugin updates.',linkBtn('View updates','plugins.html?tab=updates','puzzle','sm'))}</div><details class="mt"><summary>Update and restart behavior</summary><p>The native app must finish or pause active recording and setup before restarting. This demo shows the review and progress states without restarting your computer’s app.</p></details>`;
default:return `<div class="notice ${state.setup?'green':''} mb"><div class="flex"><span class="${state.setup?'success':'accent'}">${icon(state.setup?'check':'spark')}</span><div><strong>${state.setup?'You’re ready to go.':'Choose how you want to work.'}</strong><br>${state.setup?'Your workspace tools are configured. You can check, repair or change them here.':'Set up your preferred AI path. Your notes, calendar and plugins work independently of the CodeMie platform.'}</div></div></div><div class="grid2 mb"><button class="setup-choice ${state.mode==='direct'?'selected':''}" data-action="mode:direct"><div class="round-icon">${icon('terminal')}</div><div><h3>Direct Claude Code ${state.mode==='direct'?tag('SELECTED','purple'):''}</h3><p>Use your own Claude Code sign-in. No CodeMie account or CLI required.</p></div></button><button class="setup-choice ${state.mode==='codemie'?'selected':''}" data-action="mode:codemie"><div class="round-icon blue">${icon('globe')}</div><div><h3>Through CodeMie ${state.mode==='codemie'?tag('SELECTED','purple'):''}</h3><p>Platform models, project context and assistants. Or configure your own key or Ollama in CLI setup.</p></div></button></div><div class="panel panel-pad">${(state.mode==='direct'?[['Detect Claude Code',state.claude?'An existing installation was found.':'Install the tool into your user environment.'],['Verify your sign-in','Use the account already configured in Claude Code.'],['Choose your workspace profile','Keep your own session, skills and environment.']]:[['Prepare the runtime',state.cli?'CodeMie CLI is available.':'Use an existing CLI or prepare the app-managed Node and CLI.'],['Configure CodeMie','Choose SSO and a project, your own key, or a local provider.'],['Install Claude Code engine','Reuse the current Connect installation flow.'],['Validate installation','Run doctor and verify the selected account.']]).map(([t,d],i)=>`<div class="step"><div class="step-num ${state.setup?'complete':''}">${state.setup?icon('check'):i+1}</div><div class="grow"><h3>${t}</h3><p>${d}</p></div>${state.setup?tag('Ready','green'):''}</div>`).join('')}<div class="flex mt">${btn(state.setup?'Run setup again':'Start setup','start-setup','arrow','primary')}${btn('Simulate a setup issue','simulate-setup-error','info','ghost sm')}</div></div><details class="mt"><summary>Advanced setup and existing installs</summary><p>Keep existing CLI detection, login-shell PATH discovery, bundled runtime preparation, interactive terminal prompts, approval gates, cancellation and retry. Setup is moved, not rewritten. Direct Claude does not invoke CodeMie setup.</p></details>`}}
pages['settings-ai']=()=>settingsShell(`<h2>AI profiles</h2><p class="intro">Choose where each conversation and routine runs. Your workspace doesn’t require a platform account.</p><div class="panel mb">${settingRow('Default profile','Used for new conversations. Existing sessions keep their own profile.',`<select aria-label="Default AI profile" data-preference="mode"><option value="direct" ${state.mode==='direct'?'selected':''}>Direct Claude Code</option><option value="codemie" ${state.mode==='codemie'?'selected':''}>CodeMie · Personal project</option></select>`)}</div><div class="panel panel-pad mb"><div class="flex"><div class="round-icon">${icon('terminal')}</div><div class="grow"><h3>Direct Claude Code</h3><p class="small">Your subscription · your existing local sign-in</p></div>${tag(state.claude?'Ready':'Needs setup',state.claude?'green':'amber')}</div><div class="line"></div><div class="grid2"><div><div class="kicker">CONNECTION</div><p class="small mt" style="margin-top:9px">Native Claude Code process<br>Personal skills and working folder</p></div><div><div class="kicker">DEFAULT MODEL</div><select class="mt" style="margin-top:8px" data-preference="directModel" aria-label="Direct Claude model"><option>Account default</option><option ${state.directModel==='Fast'?'selected':''}>Fast</option><option ${state.directModel==='Reasoning'?'selected':''}>Reasoning</option></select></div></div><div class="flex mt">${btn('Test profile','test-profile:direct','play','sm')}${linkBtn('Configure tool','settings-setup.html#tools','settings','sm')}</div></div><div class="panel panel-pad"><div class="flex"><div class="round-icon blue">${icon('globe')}</div><div class="grow"><h3>CodeMie · Personal project</h3><p class="small">Platform models, assistants and project budget</p></div>${tag(state.platformConnected?'Connected':'Optional',state.platformConnected?'green':'')}</div><div class="line"></div>${field('Platform URL','platform-url',state.platformUrl||'https://codemie.lab.epam.com','','url')}<div class="grid2">${field('Project','platform-project',state.platformProject||'Personal project')}${selectField('Model','platform-model',['Project default','Fast','Reasoning'],state.platformModel||'Project default')}</div><div class="flex">${btn(state.platformConnected?'Test connection':'Connect CodeMie','connect-platform','link','primary')}${btn('Save profile','save-platform','check')}</div></div><details class="mt"><summary>Profile and plugin behavior</summary><p>Each session and routine pins its profile. Echo-compatible plugins use ctx.claude.run with the selected profile. CodeMie assistants appear only when the platform is connected. Claude-specific plugins still require Claude Code; selecting a different coding tool does not provide that service.</p></details>`);
const graphCapabilities=[['calendar','calendar','Calendar','Your meetings and meeting links','Calendars.Read'],['mail','mail','Outlook mail','Read mail and prepare local replies','Mail.Read'],['chats','teams','Teams chats','Read the conversations you can access','Chat.Read'],['people','users','People','Useful people and meeting context','People.Read'],['files','file','OneDrive files','Find and read your files as context','Files.Read']];
pages['settings-connections']=()=>settingsShell(`<h2>Connections</h2><p class="intro">Connect the services that add useful context. Pick each capability separately.</p><section class="panel panel-pad"><div class="flex"><div class="integration-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="grow"><h3>Microsoft 365</h3><p class="small">Calendar, Outlook, Teams, people and OneDrive · Microsoft Graph</p></div>${tag(({connected:'Connected',disconnected:'Not connected',expired:'Sign-in expired',blocked:'Admin approval needed'})[state.graph],state.graph==='connected'?'green':state.graph==='disconnected'?'':'amber')}</div>${state.graph==='expired'?'<div class="notice amber mt"><strong>Your Microsoft sign-in needs refreshing.</strong> Your cached agenda remains available. Reconnect to sync new items.</div>':''}${state.graph==='blocked'?'<div class="notice amber mt"><strong>Your organization requires admin approval.</strong> Calendar and local workspace features remain available from cached data. Review requested permissions or use your organization’s app registration.</div>':''}<div class="line"></div>${state.graph==='connected'?'<div class="between small mb"><span>Demo account · you@example.com</span><span class="dim">Last sync: 09:40 · 2 min ago</span></div>':''}<div>${graphCapabilities.map(([id,ico,t,d,scope])=>`<div class="setting-row" style="padding-left:0;padding-right:0"><div class="round-icon ${id==='chats'?'blue':''}">${icon(ico)}</div><div class="grow"><h3>${t}</h3><p>${d}</p></div>${tag(state.graph==='connected'&&state.graphScopes.includes(id)?'Enabled':'Not connected',state.graph==='connected'&&state.graphScopes.includes(id)?'green':'')}</div>`).join('')}</div><div class="flex mt wrap">${btn(state.graph==='connected'?'Manage capabilities':'Connect Microsoft 365','graph-connect','link','primary')}${state.graph==='connected'?btn('Sync now','graph-sync','refresh')+btn('Disconnect','graph-disconnect','','ghost'):''}${state.graph==='blocked'?btn('View admin request','graph-admin','external'):''}</div></section><div class="notice mt"><strong>Reading and sending are separate permissions.</strong> Mail.Send, ChatMessage.Send and calendar write access are requested only when you enable their actions. ${state.graphSend?'Sending is enabled for demo review flows.':'Sending is currently off.'} ${btn(state.graphSend?'Manage sending':'Enable send actions','graph-enable-send','shield','ghost sm')}</div><details class="mt"><summary>Organization setup and advanced options</summary><p>Use system-browser sign-in with PKCE. Your organization may restrict consent, Teams access or app registrations. A read-only calendar connection does not grant mail, file or send access.</p>${field('Application client ID (optional)','graph-client-id',state.graphClientId||'','Use your organization’s public client ID')}${field('Tenant','graph-tenant',state.graphTenant||'common')}${btn('Save registration','save-graph-registration','check','sm')}</details><div class="section-title"><h2>More connections</h2></div><div class="panel">${settingRow('Obsidian vaults','Connect local Markdown vaults through the Echo-compatible plugin.',linkBtn('Configure','plugin.html?id=obsidian','gem','sm'))}${settingRow('GitHub','Reuse the computer’s GitHub sign-in, or sign in through the plugin.',linkBtn('Configure','plugin.html?id=github','github','sm'))}${settingRow('Telegram','Bring your own bot through the Echo-compatible plugin.',linkBtn('Explore','plugin.html?id=telegram','telegram','sm'))}</div>`);
pages['settings-appearance']=()=>settingsShell(`<h2>Appearance</h2><p class="intro">Quiet by default. Yours in the details.</p><div class="section-title"><h2>Theme</h2><span class="small dim">Synced across every page</span></div><div class="grid3">${['light','dark','system'].map(t=>`<button class="theme-card ${state.theme===t?'active':''}" data-action="set-theme:${t}"><div class="theme-preview ${t}"><i></i><i></i></div><div class="between small"><strong>${t[0].toUpperCase()+t.slice(1)}</strong>${state.theme===t?icon('check'):''}</div></button>`).join('')}</div><div class="panel mt">${settingRow('Accent color','A little personality, without getting in your way.',`<div class="flex">${[['violet','#7760db'],['blue','#5482d9'],['teal','#338c7e']].map(([c,v])=>`<button class="color-dot ${state.accent===c?'active':''}" style="--swatch:${v}" data-action="accent:${c}" aria-label="${c} accent"></button>`).join('')}</div>`)}${settingRow('Density','Choose a little more space or a little more information.',`<select data-preference="density" aria-label="Density"><option value="comfortable" ${state.density==='comfortable'?'selected':''}>Comfortable</option><option value="compact" ${state.density==='compact'?'selected':''}>Compact</option></select>`)}${settingRow('Sidebar','Keep labels visible, or save a little space.',`<select data-preference="sidebar" aria-label="Sidebar style"><option value="expanded" ${state.sidebar==='expanded'?'selected':''}>Expanded</option><option value="compact" ${state.sidebar==='compact'?'selected':''}>Icons only</option></select>`)}${settingRow('Today layout','Pick the widgets and order that help you most.',btn('Customize Today','customize-today','sliders','sm'))}</div><div class="notice mt">Themes apply across your workspace. Compatible plugin views follow the same appearance, so new capabilities feel at home.</div>`);
pages['settings-privacy']=()=>settingsShell(`<h2>Privacy & permissions</h2><p class="intro">A clear view of what is local, what is shared, and who can access it.</p><div class="notice green mb"><strong>${icon('shield')} Local first, by design.</strong> This prototype uses fictional data in your browser. The planned native workspace keeps files locally and sends only selected context to the chosen AI profile.</div><div class="panel">${settingRow('Recording','Ask before every meeting recording. Never start recording from a calendar invitation alone.',tag('Always ask','green'))}${settingRow('AI context','Review the sources and profile before starting a conversation.',linkBtn('AI profiles','settings-ai.html','spark','sm'))}${settingRow('Microsoft 365','Access only the capabilities you connect; outward actions get their own review.',linkBtn('Manage','settings-connections.html','link','sm'))}${settingRow('Plugin permissions','Each package declares its access. Updates adding access need a new review.',linkBtn('Review plugins','plugins.html?tab=installed','puzzle','sm'))}${settingRow('Usage reporting','Keep workspace usage summaries on this device.',toggle('localAnalytics','Local usage summaries',state.localAnalytics!==false))}</div><div class="section-title"><h2>System access</h2><span class="small dim">Native implementation proposal</span></div><div class="panel">${settingRow('Microphone & system audio','Required only for recording. Granted through macOS or Windows system settings.',btn('Review access','system-permissions','mic','sm'))}${settingRow('Granted folders','Personal knowledge · read and write by reviewed actions. Plugin grants remain separate.',btn('Manage folders','folder-grants','folder','sm'))}${settingRow('Activity history','See tool actions, connection changes and approved operations.',linkBtn('View log','settings-setup.html#logs','list','sm'))}</div><details class="mt"><summary>What plugin permissions can and cannot guarantee</summary><p>Echo’s host validates declared services, folder boundaries and network hosts. Package scripts run with user rights, and client JavaScript is trusted code in the window. Full reuse must retain that trust model explicitly; a manifest is not an OS sandbox. Stronger isolation needs a separate extension contract.</p></details>`);
